eli: Quick sync — proposing a header-based client feature gate for the SDK cache experiment. Idea: clients add a header `X-RW-SDK-Flags: sdk_cache_v2=on` and we let server routes opt into cache behavior if client version >= 1.8.0. Need canary audiences, rollout guardrails, and clear fallback for older clients. Thoughts?

nicole: +1 on header approach. A couple q's: 1) header name — should we namespace (`x-rw-sdk-flags`) vs short (`x-rw-f`)? proxies sometimes strip weird headers. 2) docs/update cadence — we'll need changelog + SDK release notes. :memo:

raj: For fallback: server MUST ignore header for clients that don't send `X-RW-SDK-Version` or whose semver < 1.8.0. If header present but malformed => log at warn and ignore. Proposed semver match: `/^1\.(8|9|[2-9][0-9])(?:\.|$)/`. Also consider sending `x-rw-sdk-version` separately to avoid parsing flags for version.

pat: Rollout plan idea: 0.5% (smoke, 1h) -> 5% (24h) -> 25% (48h) -> 100%. Canary audiences: internal accounts + small subset of paid customers by revenue bracket. Metrics to watch: 99th latency, p95, error rate, cache hit rate, avg tokens/request, downstream DB QPS. If any metric regress >10% we pause and rollback. :eyes:

ci-bot: CI update: canary PR #428 ran unit + integration. Unit + integ passed. E2E flagged header-drop in our nginx staging config (strip_unknown_headers=true). See: https://ci.internal/runs/428 — failing test reproduces header drop.

qa-jun: Repro notes from e2e: when header contains multiple flags (`sdk_cache_v2=on,feature_x=off`) our parser crashed on the whitespace. Fix: split on `/,\s*/`. Also watch for duplicate keys — last-one-wins. Added test case in local harness.

eli: Good catch. Example Node snippet we should land in SDK and server docs:

```
// parse X-RW-SDK-Flags
const raw = req.headers['x-rw-sdk-flags'] || '';
const flags = raw.split(/,\s*/).reduce((acc, kv) => {
  const [k,v] = kv.split('=');
  if (!k) return acc;
  acc[k.trim()] = (v === undefined) ? true : v.trim();
  return acc;
}, {});
// feature enabled only if client ok
const ver = req.headers['x-rw-sdk-version'] || '0.0.0';
if (semver.satisfies(ver, '>=1.8.0') && flags['sdk_cache_v2'] === 'on') {
  enableCacheForRequest(req);
}
```

nicole: We'll need an entry in the SDK migration guide and a short blurb in the HTTP header policy (call out proxies and cloudloadbalancers). I'll pick up docs.

pat: Also add a server-side kill-switch: remote-config flag `sdk_cache_v2_enabled_global = false` so we can disable regardless of headers. Add alert on rollout when cache hit rate drops > 15% vs baseline.

raj: Ops note: nginx config in front of gateway must set `proxy_set_header X-RW-SDK-Flags $http_x_rw_sdk_flags;` and `underscores_in_headers on;` where needed. We'll create a deploy checklist item.

ci-bot: Action items created: ticket INF-1122 (nginx tweak), SDK-985 (parser + version header), ROLLOUT-77 (canary plan). Links: https://tickets/internal/INF-1122, https://tickets/internal/SDK-985

eli: Plan for me: I'll open server PR today with header parsing + safe defaults, add telemetry event `sdk_flag_evaluated` with fields [flag, client_version, decision, reason]. @nicole please draft docs. @pat please own rollout schedule + alert thresholds. Target: merge by EOD tomorrow, start 0.5% canary Thursday. :shipit:

nicole: ack, will draft.

pat: ack. I'll sync with SRE on alerting.

raj: I'll take the nginx change + test harness.

qa-jun: I'll run the canary test matrix once PRs are up.

eli: thanks all — I'll ping again once PRs are linked. :tada:
